IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-licensee-duties`
IMPORT `g3-training-duty`
IMPORT `g3-operator`

-- g3-tests-red.l4: assertions that are MEANT TO FAIL, written by ENCODER G3.  Each one states the answer of a REJECTED reading of a fork and
-- puts it to the function of the reading TAKEN, so each fails exactly where the two readings part.  Every one has a twin in the passing test
-- modules that asserts the same answer of the alternative function (so the alternative really gives it).  There are 19 of them: check.sh
-- lists this module with expected_failed 19, and a count other than 19 (a red assertion that went green, or an error) is a defect.
-- That this file can fail at all is the proof that the harness reads failures.

§ `Assertions that are meant to fail`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`red fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2026 3 31

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`red fixture — 30 June 2030 is a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2030 6 30

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`red fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` MEANS LIST `grade 2 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`red fixture — grade 1 only` MEANS LIST `grade 1 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`red fixture — no kind` MEANS EMPTY

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`red fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` MEANS LIST `grade 2 licence`, `grade 3 licence`

GIVETH A `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`red fixture — wording of 2020, all conformed` MEANS `Wording of Israeli Standard 994` WITH
    `the day this wording took effect` IS YMD 2020 1 1
    `the work conformed to part 4 of this wording` IS TRUE
    `a tightness test of the refrigerant piping was performed as the testing chapter of part 4 of this wording requires` IS TRUE
    `the work conformed to part 5 of this wording` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`red fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test` MEANS `Wording of Israeli Standard 994` WITH
    `the day this wording took effect` IS YMD 2020 1 1
    `the work conformed to part 4 of this wording` IS FALSE
    `a tightness test of the refrigerant piping was performed as the testing chapter of part 4 of this wording requires` IS FALSE
    `the work conformed to part 5 of this wording` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Work item`
`red fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` MEANS `Work item` WITH
    `performed by` IS (Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "IL-100", `kind of person` IS `an individual`)
    `the kind of job` IS `an installation job`
    `the system` IS (`Cooling system` WITH `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS 25, `refrigerants` IS EMPTY)
    `date performed` IS YMD 2026 3 10

GIVETH A `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`red fixture — wording of 2026, part 5 not met` MEANS `Wording of Israeli Standard 994` WITH
    `the day this wording took effect` IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the work conformed to part 4 of this wording` IS TRUE
    `a tightness test of the refrigerant piping was performed as the testing chapter of part 4 of this wording requires` IS TRUE
    `the work conformed to part 5 of this wording` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Work item`
`red fixture — installation on 31 December 2025` MEANS `Work item` WITH
    `performed by` IS (Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "IL-100", `kind of person` IS `an individual`)
    `the kind of job` IS `an installation job`
    `the system` IS (`Cooling system` WITH `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS 25, `refrigerants` IS EMPTY)
    `date performed` IS YMD 2025 12 31

GIVEN day IS A DATE
      hours IS A NUMBER
      supervised IS A BOOLEAN
      recognised IS A BOOLEAN
      infield IS A BOOLEAN
      directed IS A BOOLEAN
      required IS A BOOLEAN
      met IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Training session attended`
`red fixture — a session` day hours supervised recognised infield directed required met MEANS
    `Training session attended` WITH
        `the day attended` IS day
        `the licence was in force on the day attended` IS TRUE
        `hours attended` IS hours
        `held under the supervision of the Ministry` IS supervised
        `conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division` IS recognised
        `within the licensee's field of work under the licence` IS infield
        `held on a date the Registrar directed` IS directed
        `attended because the Registrar required that particular course under section 17(b)` IS required
        `the licensee met the requirements of the training` IS met

GIVEN `the day of the course` IS A DATE
      `the day notice of the requirement was given` IS A DATE
      reasonable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Particular course required under section 17(b)`
`red fixture — a course` `the day of the course` `the day notice of the requirement was given` reasonable MEANS
    `Particular course required under section 17(b)` WITH
        `the day of the course` IS `the day of the course`
        `the day notice of the requirement was given` IS `the day notice of the requirement was given`
        `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division` IS TRUE
        `the Council was consulted about requiring the course` IS TRUE
        `the Council's advice about requiring the course was validly given` IS TRUE
        `in the Registrar's opinion circumstances justify requiring attendance` IS TRUE
        `in the Registrar's opinion attendance is required to train the licensee and to realise the purposes of the Law` IS TRUE
        `notice was given a reasonable time before the date of the course` IS reasonable
        `the licensee attended the course` IS FALSE
        `the licensee met the requirements of the course` IS FALSE

GIVEN `the day of the Registrar's decision` IS A DATE
      original IS A DATE
      current IS A DATE
      fixed IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Extension of validity under section 17(c)`
`red fixture — an extension` `the day of the Registrar's decision` original current fixed MEANS
    `Extension of validity under section 17(c)` WITH
        `the day of the Registrar's decision` IS `the day of the Registrar's decision`
        `the last day of validity before any extension under section 17(c)` IS original
        `the last day of validity as it stands when the decision is taken` IS current
        `the last day of validity fixed by the extension` IS fixed
        `the licensee had not fulfilled the duty under section 17(a) or (b)` IS TRUE
        `the Council was consulted about the extension` IS TRUE
        `the Council's advice about the extension was validly given` IS TRUE
        `in the Registrar's opinion these are special cases and the circumstances are justified` IS TRUE
        `the extension is granted so that the licensee can fulfil the duty` IS TRUE

GIVEN regular IS A BOOLEAN
      business IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
`red fixture — a person who` regular `and` business MEANS
    `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems` WITH
        `engages another person on a regular basis to perform work on cooling systems` IS regular
        `owns or manages a business that offers the performance of work on cooling systems to the public` IS business

GIVEN sufficient IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Measures the operator took under section 18(b)`
`red fixture — measures` sufficient MEANS
    `Measures the operator took under section 18(b)` WITH
        `the measures were sufficient to make sure that the licensee would work to the Standard` IS sufficient

GIVEN hours IS A NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Training session attended`
`red fixture — a qualifying session` hours day MEANS `red fixture — a session` day hours TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE

§§ `The rejected readings, put to the readings taken`

-- R1 (fork S16, kind D): without IL s.10(c) the last day for notifying a change of 1 March 2026 is 31 March even when 31 March is a day of rest.
-- The reading taken applies IL s.10(c) and answers 1 April.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `red fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
-- R2 (fork S16): on that reading a notice of 1 April 2026 is late.  The reading taken says it is in time.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`Change in the application particulars` WITH `the particular was one the licensee gave in a licence application` IS TRUE, `the day of the change` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `the Registrar directed a manner of notifying` IS FALSE, `the notice followed the manner the Registrar directed` IS FALSE, `the day the notice was given to the Registrar` IS JUST (YMD 2026 4 1)) `red fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest`
-- R3 (fork S13a): judged against the wording in force on the day of the inspection (June 2026), a work of 31 December 2025 breaches section 13.
-- The reading taken judges it against the wording of the day of the work, the 2020 wording, which it met.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `red fixture — installation on 31 December 2025` (LIST `red fixture — wording of 2020, all conformed`, `red fixture — wording of 2026, part 5 not met`) TRUE `red fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- R4 (fork S17-A): the last year counted back from the extended last day excludes a session of 10 April 2029; the reading taken still counts it.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `red fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 4 10)) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30)
-- R5 (fork S17-C): a course required under (b) counts towards the eight hours.  The reading taken excludes it.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `red fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31)
-- R6 (fork S17-D): requirements bind only the sessions counted towards the eight hours, so eight met hours plus two unmet qualifying hours is enough.
-- The reading taken binds every qualifying session.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `red fixture — a qualifying session` 8 (YMD 2029 10 1), `red fixture — a session` (YMD 2029 11 1) 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31)
-- R7 (fork S17-E): a licensee who attended nothing is excused when no qualifying training was available.  The reading taken has no excuse.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` EMPTY (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31)
-- R8 (fork S17-F): the licensee must attend the course although notice was not given a reasonable time before.  The reading taken makes reasonable notice
-- a condition of his duty.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.17(b) — the licensee must attend the course` (`red fixture — a course` (YMD 2027 6 10) (YMD 2027 6 9) FALSE) TRUE
-- R9 (fork S17-V): with IL s.10(c) applied to the cap, three months from 31 March 2030 is 1 July 2030 when 30 June is a day of rest.
-- The reading taken (kind V: IL s.10(c) not applied) answers 30 June.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the latest last day of validity after an extension of up to three months from` (YMD 2030 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2030 7 1
-- R10 (fork S17-V2): the three months are cumulative, so a second extension to 30 September 2030 is too long.  The reading taken counts each extension
-- from the end as it stands.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`red fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 6 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30) (YMD 2030 9 30)) TRUE
-- R11 (fork S17-T): the Registrar may extend whenever he decides, even after the validity has run out.  The reading taken requires the decision on or before the last day.
-- EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`red fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 4 1) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30)) TRUE
-- R12 (fork S17-M, trap T25): the extension may not pass 31 March, the limit of section 8.  The reading taken lets it.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`red fixture — an extension` (YMD 2030 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 6 30)) TRUE
-- R13 (fork S18-H): a person whose licence is held but not in force has a licence "in his hand", so engaging him is item (6).
-- The reading taken counts only a licence in force, so it answers item (5).  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a)` (`red fixture — a person who` TRUE `and` FALSE) TRUE TRUE `red fixture — no kind` `red fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts` EQUALS JUST `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`
-- R14 (fork S18-C): the owner of a public business who does not regularly engage is not an operator.  The reading taken says he is.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(c) — the person is an operator` (`red fixture — a person who` FALSE `and` TRUE)
-- R16 (fork S13c): item (4) frozen to the wording in force on 14 January 2025, under which no tightness test was performed, is committed by the installation of
-- 10 March 2026.  The reading taken judges the test against the wording of the day of the work, the 2026 wording, and finds no item.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13` `red fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` (LIST `red fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`, `red fixture — wording of 2026, part 5 not met`) TRUE `red fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS JUST `installation without the tightness test of the piping`
-- R17 (fork S18-D): the word operator in the Third Schedule is defined only for s.18, so the items cannot be applied and the question is refused.
-- The reading taken answers a value.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s.18(a) — the listed violation committed under section 18(a)` (`red fixture — a person who` TRUE `and` FALSE) TRUE TRUE `red fixture — no kind` `red fixture — the kinds that cover a system of 25 kilowatts`
-- R18 (fork S15b): the express duty of s.15 reaches only information or documents, so a demand for a report creates no duty.  The reading taken binds the licensee
-- to a demand for a report too.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT NOT `s.15 — the licensee must comply with the demand` (`Demand of the Registrar under section 15` WITH `the kind of demand` IS `a report on particulars of the licensee's engagement as a licensee`, `the particulars concern the licensee's engagement as a licensee` IS TRUE, `in the Registrar's opinion the information or documents are needed to realise the purposes of the Law` IS FALSE, `the demand is made as a condition for renewing or extending the licence` IS FALSE, `the day of the demand` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `the day the Registrar directed that the report or supply be made by` IS NOTHING) `red fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- R19 (fork S17-d): read as binding from the first day of the last year, the deemed condition is already breached on 1 October 2029 by a licensee with no training yet.
-- The reading taken finds a breach only when the window has closed, on 1 April 2030 or later.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.17(d) — the licence condition of section 17(a) was breached as at` (YMD 2029 10 1) EMPTY (YMD 2030 3 31) (YMD 2030 3 31) TRUE
-- R15 (fork S18-B): a duty of result is breached when the licensee's work failed the Standard even though the measures were sufficient.
-- The reading taken (conduct) finds no breach.  EXPECTED TO FAIL.
#ASSERT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b)` (`red fixture — a person who` TRUE `and` FALSE) TRUE TRUE `red fixture — grade 1 only` (`red fixture — measures` TRUE)
